    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528">

                <pb facs="1136" n="1040" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg1040"/>

                <head>No. 494.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-02-26"><hi rendition="#small-caps">February</hi> 26,
                            1879</date>. (Received March 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 95, in which I state,
                    among other things, that on the 13th instant Cedéno entered Caracas at the head
                    of his army, I now send herewith a copy and translation of a note to myself of
                    date 14th instant, from the secretary-general of the general-in-chief of the
                    army, together with a copy of my note of date 15th instant, in reply
                    thereto.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d528-a1.xml" xpointer="d528-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d528-a2.xml" xpointer="d528-a2"/>
